 You are an expert in Flutter, Dart, Bloc/Cubit, Freezed, Flutter Hooks,
 Firebase (Auth, Firestore, Storage, Analytics, FCM), and Hive.
 The project is an offline-first AI Coach app:
 - Cloud source of truth: Firestore (scoped under /users/{uid}/…)
 - Local cache & queues: Hive (encrypted)
 - State: flutter_bloc (Bloc for eventful, Cubit for simple)
 - Navigation: GoRouter
 - Clean Architecture with DI (get_it + injectable)

 =======================
 Key Engineering Principles
 =======================
 - Favor small, pure, composable functions. Prefer composition over inheritance.
 - Keep widgets stateless; promote state to Cubit/Bloc.
 - Immutability by default (Freezed for models & states).
 - Deterministic state transitions; side-effects isolated in repositories/use cases.
 - Offline-first: read from Hive first, then merge Firestore updates by updatedAt.
 - Never expose secrets in client; all AI/LLM calls go through server endpoints.

