 =======================
 Dart/Flutter Conventions
 =======================
 - Use const constructors for immutable widgets.
 - Use arrow syntax for simple methods; one-line getters/setters as expression bodies.
 - Use trailing commas for readable diffs; keep lines ≤ 80 chars.
 - Descriptive names with auxiliaries: isLoading, hasError, canSubmit.
 - Prefer SizedBox.shrink() over Container() when no decoration needed.
 - Always include errorBuilder in Image.network.

 =======================
 State Management (Bloc/Cubit)
 =======================
 - Cubit for local/simple state (form, toggles, filters).
 - Bloc for event-driven flows (auth, plan generation, sync).
 - Use Freezed to define union states; never mutate state in place.
 - Access via context.read<T>() / context.watch<T>().
 - Keep side-effects (I/O) in repositories; Bloc only orchestrates.

 Example (Cubit + Freezed):
 ```dart
 @freezed
 class TodayState with _$TodayState {
   const factory TodayState.loading() = _Loading;
   const factory TodayState.data({
     required DateTime date,
     required List<Task> tasks,
   }) = _Data;
   const factory TodayState.failure(String message) = _Failure;
 }

 class TodayCubit extends Cubit<TodayState> {
   TodayCubit(this._repo, this._clock) : super(const TodayState.loading());
   final TaskRepository _repo;
   final DateTime Function() _clock;

   Future<void> load() async {
     emit(const TodayState.loading());
     final d = DateTime.now();
     final res = await _repo.getTasksForDate(d);
     res.fold(
       (e) => emit(TodayState.failure(e.message)),
       (tasks) => emit(TodayState.data(date: d, tasks: tasks)),
     );
   }
 }
 ```

 =======================
 Error Handling & Validation
 =======================
 - Represent failures in Cubit/Bloc states; never throw into the UI layer.
 - Display errors inline using SelectableText.rich (red) instead of SnackBars.
 - Always include empty states within the same screen.
 - Wrap async UI with BlocBuilder + small dedicated error widgets.

 Example (error text):
 ```dart
 class ErrorText extends StatelessWidget {
   const ErrorText(this.message, {super.key});
   final String message;
   @override
   Widget build(BuildContext context) => SelectableText.rich(
     TextSpan(
       text: message,
       style: Theme.of(context).textTheme.bodyMedium?.copyWith(
             color: Colors.red,
             fontWeight: FontWeight.w600,
           ),
     ),
   );
 }
 ```

 =======================
 Navigation
 =======================
 - Use GoRouter for routes & deep links. Keep route names typed.
 - Navigation side-effects live in BlocListener (not in build()).

 =======================
 Firebase Integration
 =======================
 - Auth: Firebase Authentication (Google/Email).
 - Database: Cloud Firestore with structured, normalized documents
   under /users/{uid}/…; include createdAt, updatedAt, isDeleted.
 - Storage: Firebase Storage for user files; path under /users/{uid}/….
 - Analytics: Firebase Analytics events for major flows (login, plan_generate).
 - FCM: Topic/user-scoped notifications; request permissions on onboarding.

 Security Rules (Firestore):
 ```
 rules_version = '2';
 service cloud.firestore {
   match /databases/{database}/documents {
     function isOwner(uid) {
       return request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == uid;
     }

     match /users/{userId} {
       allow read, write: if isOwner(userId);
       match /{sub=**} { allow read, write: if isOwner(userId); }
     }

     match /{document=**} { allow read, write: if false; }
   }
 }
 ```

 Storage Rules (scoped user access):
 ```
 rules_version = '2';
 service firebase.storage {
   match /b/{bucket}/o {
     function isOwner(uid) {
       return request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == uid;
     }
     match /users/{userId}/{allPaths=**} {
       allow read, write: if isOwner(userId);
     }
   }
 }
 ```

 Query Performance:
 - Use indexes for composite where/orderBy.
 - Always limit() and paginate (startAfterDocument).
 - Store denormalized counters/snapshots for dashboards.

 =======================
 Hive (Offline-first) Guidelines
 =======================
 - Use separate boxes per aggregate root: 'goals', 'tasks', 'messages'.
 - Generate TypeAdapters; bump typeId carefully (no reuse).
 - Encrypt boxes with a secure key in flutter_secure_storage.
 - Persist updatedAt in UTC; merge strategy: newest wins.
 - Maintain an "outbox" box for pending writes to Firestore on reconnect.

 Example (Hive init):
 ```dart
 final key = await _secure.read(key: 'hive_key') ??
   (await _generateAndStoreKey());
 await Hive.initFlutter();
 await Hive.openBox('goals', encryptionCipher: HiveAesCipher(key));
 await Hive.openBox('tasks', encryptionCipher: HiveAesCipher(key));
 ```

 =======================
 Data & Model Conventions
 =======================
 - Domain Entities are pure Freezed classes.
 - DTOs use json_serializable with snake_case fields.
 - Include createdAt, updatedAt, isDeleted in Firestore documents.
 - @JsonKey(includeFromJson: true, includeToJson: false) for read-only fields.
 - Enums persisted with @JsonValue(int).

 Example (DTO):
 ```dart
 @JsonSerializable(fieldRename: FieldRename.snake, explicitToJson: true)
 class TaskDto {
   final String id;
   final String goalId;
   final String title;
   final String description;
   final String date; // ISO8601 day
   final int estimatedMinutes;
   final String status; // todo|done|skipped
   final String createdAt;
   final String updatedAt;
   final bool isDeleted;

   const TaskDto({/* all required */});
   factory TaskDto.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json)
     => _$TaskDtoFromJson(json);
   Map<String, dynamic> toJson() => _$TaskDtoToJson(this);
 }
 ```

 =======================
 Repositories & Data Sources
 =======================
 - Repository abstracts domain operations (getTodayTasks, toggleDone).
 - LocalDataSource: Hive; RemoteDataSource: Firestore.
 - Sync policy:
   1) Read local immediately.
   2) Fetch remote; merge by updatedAt; write back to local.
   3) Outbox retries on connectivity changes.

 =======================
 Error Types
 =======================
 - Define Failure types (NetworkFailure, AuthFailure, StorageFailure).
 - Never leak platform exceptions to UI; map to Failure with message+code.
 - Log with dart:developer log, not print.

 =======================
 UI & Styling
 =======================
 - Use Theme extensions; prefer Theme.of(context).textTheme.titleLarge
   and headlineSmall etc. Avoid deprecated typography.
 - Responsive with LayoutBuilder/MediaQuery; avoid magic numbers.
 - Use RefreshIndicator for pull-to-refresh on list screens.
 - TextFields: set capitalization, keyboardType, textInputAction properly.

 =======================
 Notifications
 =======================
 - Local: schedule with flutter_local_notifications from Task.date/time.
 - Push: FCM for server-driven reminders and plan updates.
 - All notification taps navigate via GoRouter named routes.

 =======================
 Performance
 =======================
 - const widgets wherever possible; avoid rebuilding large trees.
 - Use ListView.builder/SliverList for long lists.
 - Cache images (AssetImage, cached_network_image).
 - Batch Firestore writes; debounce rapid updates.

 =======================
 Code Generation
 =======================
